    {
      "bbox": [
        327,
        1443,
        1867,
        1641
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "You have requested my advice as to whether a\nCity department head may continue to act as a director\nof a corporation after his appointment. Charter Section\n1100, as amended, reads as follows:",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2819,
          "min": -1.6463
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0012,
          "min": -0.0012
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 43,
          "mean": -0.0166,
          "min": -0.7007
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 4542,
        "area_px": 308000,
        "density": 0.01475,
        "chars": 191,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 42.05
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        467,
        1671,
        1775,
        1957
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "\"Every head of an administration, or department, or elected officer, except councilmen, who receives a salary from the City shall give his whole time to his duties and shall not engage in any other occupation, profession or employment.\"",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2773,
          "min": -1.4759
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0001
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 46,
          "mean": -0.0184,
          "min": -0.6932
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 8208,
        "area_px": 375396,
        "density": 0.02186,
        "chars": 236,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 28.75
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        306,
        2004,
        1989,
        2382
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "In construing similar provisions of law applicable to other officers, the courts have held that such provisions do not bar outside activities which do not involve an active management of the business or profession and which do not require an officer to devote a substantial amount of his time thereto. (In Matter of Deuel, 127 App. Div. 640, 1st Dept., 1908; Matter of Levy, 198 App. Div. 326, 1st Dept., 1921; McQuade v. Stoneham, 263 N.Y. 323.)",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2872,
          "min": -1.5067
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 133,
          "mean": -0.0144,
          "min": -0.9926
        }
      },
